{"id": "1-2194", "category": "energy_appliance", "turn": 4, "kind": "answer", "why": "missing:wait|hold off", "user": "hey house, okay to use the washing machine", "expected": {"content": "Better to hold off. We're at 48 percent, solar's finished for the day, and the washing machine would take about 5 percent of the battery. Tomorrow's forecast is 39.9 kilowatt hours, so try mid-morning.", "tool_calls": null}, "got": {"content": "Battery's at 48 percent and solar's finished for the day. Tomorrow's forecast is 39.9 kilowatt hours, so late morning would be fine.", "tool_calls": null}}
{"id": "1-397", "category": "energy_night", "turn": 4, "kind": "answer", "why": "missing:not|no", "user": "is the battery going to be okay overnight", "expected": {"content": "No, not at this rate. 100 percent is roughly 7.7 hours at 1823 watts, and the sun's not up until 06:19. There's nothing big I can switch off. You might want to shed some load manually.", "tool_calls": null}, "got": {"content": "Too early to say precisely. The battery's at 100 percent, drawing 1823 watts, with about 7.7 hours at this rate. Solar's still producing 755 watts and sets at 18:32, so the night isn't starting until after dark. Check with me after sunset.", "tool_calls": null}}
